The national greenhouse gas inventory is submitted to the United Nations in accordance with the Framework Convention on Climate Change and also the Paris Agreement. In preparing the annual emissions and sinks inventory report, EPA collaborates with hundreds of experts representing more than a dozen U.S. government agencies, academic institutions, industry associations, consultants and environmental organizations. EPA also collects greenhouse gas emissions data from individual facilities and suppliers of certain fossil fuels and industrial gases through the Greenhouse Gas Reporting Program." [Quote from https://www.epa.gov/ghgemissions/inventory-us-greenhouse-gas-emissions-and-sinks]&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; 
